ort forward and use a different port externally, then forward to 80/443 internally.  Need to get a static IP address from Gunthers to whitelist so we don't open this device up to the whole internet.","chargeToId":714038,"actualHours":0.5,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #714038","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T13:00:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T11:48:00.000Z","notes":"Reviewed logs, found there were a lot of different STP events starting around 2pm, but most of those don't correlate into a big network event. Ran logs through synthreo, it identified a gap between 23:05 and 02:00 the next morning. Checked in with Jordan, that corresponds to the outage they reported.  Checked on the watchguard and confirmed that it was offline \\(no logs in WG Cloud\\) during that same period as well. Updated Jordan.","chargeToId":718146,"actualHours":1.2,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #718146","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T13:30:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T13:00:00.000Z","notes":"Worked with Mat to review the P2P wifi, looks like it's still active but seeing lot throughput. Restarted each of the link.","chargeToId":718200,"actualHours":0.5,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #718200","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T14:00:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T13:30:00.000Z","notes":"Off Clock","chargeToId":72,"actualHours":0,"hoursDeduct":0.5,"chargecode":"97 - Off Clock (deduct field)","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T15:12:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T14:00:00.000Z","notes":"Called with Christina and Val, discussed what they're needing to accomplish and prep an initial research plan. Reviewed some of the documentation available on Claude's website. Prepped and sent call recap to Val, Christina, and Tyson.","chargeToId":717245,"actualHours":1.2,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #717245","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T15:12:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T15:00:00.000Z","notes":"Reviewed issue with Jordan, sounds like there's 5 overall devices, so as long as the vendor uses a browser to access we can do a port forward with port translation and use a single public IP. Also need to get their office public IP to lock down the port forward.","chargeToId":714038,"actualHours":0.2,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #714038","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T15:48:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T15:30:00.000Z","notes":"Reviewed replacement P2P APs that Mat and Jordan found, discussed deployment plans.","chargeToId":718200,"actualHours":0.3,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #718200","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T16:06:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T15:48:00.000Z","notes":"Reviewed issues and tickets.","chargeToId":51,"actualHours":0.3,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"22.5 - Board/Ticket Planning","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T16:42:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T16:06:00.000Z","notes":"Worked with Seth to make sure FFC was in CIPP and security standards were applying correctly.","chargeToId":717591,"actualHours":0.6,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #717591","timesheetId":28560},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T17:06:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T16:42:00.000Z","notes":"Found that the outbound emails were not going through barracuda because they were from the thyroidutah.com domain, which had already been moved to a new tenant for ThyroidUtah.  Enabled the connector to send straight to the internet, disabled the barracuda connector, and restarted the transport service.  Messages went out, then rolled back changes.","chargeToId":718186,"actualHours":0.4,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #718186","timesheetId":28560}]
