[2026-06-30T21:10:43] [Persephone] Step variable: time_entries = [{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T12:51:17.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T12:42:05.000Z","notes":"=== Monitor Compatibility Review for Exam Rooms ===\n\nCall Time: Jun 30, 2026, 12:42 PM\nFrom: Kara Woods\nTo: Kender Ostlund\n\n**Issue**: Kara Woods called to confirm whether the existing monitors in the exam rooms are compatible with the NextGen requirement for a widescreen 1920x1080 display. She reported that several locations have older, square Dell monitors, and one room in the ORM office is using an extended display setup with the Acuity Pro, which she did not want showing the pick list.\n\n**Troubleshooting**: Kender Ostlund reviewed the monitor specifications and explained that the square monitors are unlikely to support the required widescreen resolution. He noted that forcing the setting would likely make the display blurry, misaligned, or cut off, and that NextGen may not support the workaround. He also checked availability for an exam room in Provo and discussed whether the rooms were configured for extended display versus duplicate/default display.\n\n**Resolution**: No final fix was implemented on the call. The likely outcome is that the square monitors will need to be replaced if they cannot support the required resolution; Kender planned to verify the exact monitor models/count and confirm compatibility.\n\n**Follow-up**: Kender will check with Tyson or use Windows-reported monitor models to build a list of installed monitors and confirm counts by location. Kara Woods will coordinate with Britney on monitor replacement decisions and may provide a location-by-location list if needed.\n\n[View call in Vight](https://app.vight.ai/calls/f4c4e23b-c3bc-4b80-916c-16c14fce451f)","chargeToId":718007,"actualHours":0.15,"hoursDeduct":null,"chargecode":"Ticket #718007","timesheetId":28566},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T14:18:07.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T12:59:38.000Z","notes":"=== New Hire Account Setup and Access Requests - Pending Vendor/Admin Follow-Up ===\n\nCall Time: Jun 30, 2026, 12:59 PM\nFrom: Robert Beran\nTo: Kender Ostlund\n\n**Issue**: Robert called for first-time workstation and account setup, requesting access to Google Drive, Gmail, Paylocity, Bookkeeper/Keeper, NetSuite, a downstairs printer, and P Drive, along with help signing into the computer.\n\n**Troubleshooting**: Kender Ostlund verified the workstation name, reset the initial sign-in password, and walked Robert through setting up multifactor authentication using AuthPoint. They had multiple setup attempts due to issues scanning/activating the token and the first Google MFA setup glitching, but eventually got Gmail/Google Drive, Keeper, Chrome sign-in, and the computer login MFA working. Kender also added the Boulder downstairs printer and confirmed P Drive access.\n\n**Resolution**: Partially resolved. Robert was successfully set up for computer sign-in, Gmail, Google Drive, Keeper, printer, and P Drive. NetSuite and Paylocity were not provisioned during the call because Kender stated there is no direct access on his side.\n\n**Follow-up**: Robert needs to contact Jessica Wilkerson for NetSuite and Paylocity access/provisioning. Kender also noted the authenticator setup may need to be switched to the company cell phone later when issued.\n\n[View call in Vight](https://app.vight.ai/calls/716de732-b256-415f-9cfa-b778180074f1)","chargeToId":718163,"actualHours":1.31,"hoursDeduct":null,"chargecode":"Ticket #718163","timesheetId":28566},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T14:44:08.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T14:39:16.000Z","notes":"=== Follow-up on computer sleep issue - pending callback ===\n\nCall Time: Jun 30, 2026, 2:39 PM\nFrom: Kender Ostlund\nTo: Nolan Black\n\n**Issue**: Kender Ostlund from Equinox IT called to follow up on Sean Wissen's computer sleep issue; the computer was reportedly not waking up properly from sleep, and Kender wanted to confirm whether the issue was still occurring before Sean went on vacation.\n\n**Troubleshooting**: No live troubleshooting was performed on the call. Nolan Black confirmed he could not directly transfer Kender to Sean, and instead offered to pass along Kender's contact information or have Sean return the call.\n\n**Resolution**: The issue remains pending. Nolan Black noted he would send Kender's information to Sean so Sean can reach out directly.\n\n**Follow-up**: Sean Wissen to contact Kender Ostlund at Equinox IT using the main number provided if needed: (801) 426-7800. Kender requested email/callback follow-up rather than interrupting Sean directly.\n\n[View call in Vight](https://app.vight.ai/calls/bbc9ca01-fc6c-4882-9557-4e9c0a836fc8)","chargeToId":717678,"actualHours":0.08,"hoursDeduct":null,"chargecode":"Ticket #717678","timesheetId":28566},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T14:55:07.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T14:46:23.000Z","notes":"=== NextGen Front Desk Shortcut and Room 3 Freeze - Resolved ===\n\nCall Time: Jun 30, 2026, 2:46 PM\nFrom: Stella Torres\nTo: Kender Ostlund\n\n**Issue**: Stella reported two issues: the front desk computer was having trouble opening the NextGen 8 shortcut, and Room 3 in Payson was frozen on a patient record and would not return to the normal application view. The Room 3 workstation was using the generic Payson Windows login, with the EHR session under Doctor Lovelace.\n\n**Troubleshooting**: Kender Ostlund confirmed the front desk NextGen issue and then verified the frozen workstation details. He identified the PC name as \"payson exam two,\" noted the system was stuck due to the CL lens code behavior, and explained this is a known issue related to square monitors/monitor compatibility with the new NextGen setup. He logged the Room 3 session out and performed a remote restart/reset to clear the stuck state.\n\n**Resolution**: The front desk NextGen issue was fixed, and the Room 3 session was released from the frozen state. Kender also noted the CL lens code behavior is expected to continue until the site gets the correct widescreen monitors.\n\n**Follow-up**: Tara is working on getting the correct monitors, and Kender is compiling a list of monitors that are too square for the new system. The site may continue to see the CL lens code issue on incompatible monitors until hardware is replaced.\n\n[View call in Vight](https://app.vight.ai/calls/c483ed11-8e91-4fab-9f6f-e3a158beaf04)","chargeToId":718238,"actualHours":0.15,"hoursDeduct":null,"chargecode":"Ticket #718238","timesheetId":28566},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T15:00:00.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T14:48:00.000Z","notes":"Called for Sean, front desk said they have been filtering his calls and he hasnt been taking any today. They took a message from me. Emailed Sean and explained I am available and asked if he is still having any issues.","chargeToId":715073,"actualHours":0.2,"hoursDeduct":0,"chargecode":"Ticket #715073","timesheetId":28566},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T16:20:33.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T16:14:07.000Z","notes":"=== Portal Link Error - Likely Vendor-Side Issue ===\n\nCall Time: Jun 30, 2026, 4:14 PM\nFrom: Brittney Wachter\nTo: Kender Ostlund\n\n**Issue**: Brittney Wachter reported she could not access a portal website from an email link and received an error when trying to open the page.\n\n**Troubleshooting**: Kender Ostlund connected remotely, cleared browser cookies, and had Brittney retry the link. He then had her try opening the portal link in Firefox instead of her original browser; the same error occurred. Kender noted the error did not match typical company-side issues and indicated it was likely related to the vendor portal, possibly an expired link or portal bug.\n\n**Resolution**: The issue was not resolved during the call. Kender concluded the problem was likely on the portal/vendor side rather than their environment.\n\n**Follow-up**: Brittney had already emailed the portal provider and planned to let them know the link/error appears to be on their end. No further action was required from Kender at that time.\n\n[View call in Vight](https://app.vight.ai/calls/6164718a-3fdc-4ad1-977a-267c778bdb6f)","chargeToId":717558,"actualHours":0.11,"hoursDeduct":null,"chargecode":"Ticket #717558","timesheetId":28566},{"timeEnd":"2026-06-30T17:39:18.000Z","timeStart":"2026-06-30T17:29:28.000Z","notes":"=== Controlled Substance Signing / Challenge Questions Issue - Escalated ===\n\nCall Time: Jun 30, 2026, 5:29 PM\nFrom: Catarina Richards\nTo: Kender Ostlund\n\n**Issue**: Catarina Richards reported that she could not send controlled substances from the Foothill Family Clinic workflow because her challenge questions appeared to have changed, and the reset flow was failing. When she attempted to access settings to reset the questions, Duo push approval opened but the reset screen would not load, leaving a blank page.\n\n**Troubleshooting**: Kender Ostlund confirmed her account details after some difficulty finding her in the system due to a name change. He observed that the challenge questions in the system appeared different from what Catarina expected and confirmed the behavior was abnormal. He checked available documentation, reviewed Duo-related support info, and attempted to locate internal access/help for the Epic admin side.\n\n**Resolution**: Issue was not resolved on the call. Kender determined he did not have access to the Epic admin settings needed to correct the challenge questions and could not directly fix the Duo/settings problem.\n\n**Follow-up**: Kender advised that Jonathan usually handles Epic admin changes and offered to contact him and/or provide the Epic support number. He found and provided the Epic support contact number to Catarina, and she planned to call support herself if needed. Catarina noted the medication could be sent the next day if the issue remained unresolved.\n\n[View call in Vight](https://app.vight.ai/calls/3421aa23-dcfd-469f-ad6b-7dd8f0e5d802)","chargeToId":718045,"actualHours":0.16,"hoursDeduct":null,"chargecode":"Ticket #718045","timesheetId":28566}]
